{
  "key_evidence_summary": "Pods listing in namespace boutique: only outlier is currencyservice-7cc975cfff-nk87k, showing 0/1 READY (all other 10 services 1/1), RESTARTS 0. Pod detail shows container port 7000/TCP with env PORT=7000, Liveness grpc <pod>:7000 (correct), but Readiness grpc <pod>:7001, Ready=False. Pod events carry the mechanism verbatim: 'Warning Unhealthy 0s (x10 over 80s) kubelet Readiness probe failed: timeout: failed to connect service \"172.20.2.130:7001\" within 1s: context deadline exceeded'. GetAppYAML confirms the misconfiguration: spec.template.spec.containers[server].readinessProbe.grpc.port = 7001 while containerPort = 7000, env PORT = 7000, livenessProbe.grpc.port = 7000 and the Service maps port 7000 -> targetPort 7000. Impact closed: endpoints/currencyservice has an empty ENDPOINTS column (109s) and CheckServiceConnectivity(currencyservice:7000) returns Connection Failed, so callers frontend/checkoutservice cannot reach the service. Restart Count 0 proves the container was never killed (liveness port is correct), localizing the first observation-vs-expectation break at the readiness probe port configuration of the currencyservice deployment carrier.",
  "top_3_predictions": [
